WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:01.901
-Thank you very much.

00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:04.100
It is Friday.
It is Fri-yay.

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:06.400
[ Cheers ]
Let's do it. Come on, now.

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:08.701
Welcome to "The Tonight Show,"
everybody.

00:00:08.701 --> 00:00:10.434
Let's get to the news and jokes.

00:00:10.434 --> 00:00:13.434
Well, guys, new polling shows
President Trump's support

00:00:13.434 --> 00:00:15.501
among senior citizens
has slipped

00:00:15.501 --> 00:00:17.767
in key battleground states,
and you could tell

00:00:17.767 --> 00:00:20.000
Trump's worried 'cause
look at what he just announced

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.167
to help win back older voters.

00:00:22.167 --> 00:00:25.667
-Under my plan, 33 million
Medicare beneficiaries

00:00:25.667 --> 00:00:30.834
will soon receive a card
in the mail containing $200

00:00:30.834 --> 00:00:33.801
that they can use to help pay
for prescription drugs.

00:00:33.801 --> 00:00:36.534
Nobody's seen this before.
These cards are incredible.

00:00:36.534 --> 00:00:39.868
The cards will be mailed out
in coming weeks.

00:00:39.868 --> 00:00:43.200
I will always take care of our
wonderful senior citizens.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.567
-Wow.
That is exciting.

00:00:45.567 --> 00:00:47.367
I mean, between the $200 card

00:00:47.367 --> 00:00:52.000
and the second COVID
stimulus check, that's $200.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:55.734
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.734 --> 00:00:58.033
I did a little Kenan Thompson,
a little...

00:00:58.033 --> 00:01:01.934
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.934 --> 00:01:05.534
I stole his move.
Kenan, I stole your move.

00:01:05.534 --> 00:01:07.934
That's right, Trump is really
pandering to seniors today.

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:11.934
He also announced that his new
attorney general is Matlock.

00:01:11.934 --> 00:01:13.601
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.601 --> 00:01:16.367
Not only that, Trump's
also changing his slogan to

00:01:16.367 --> 00:01:19.467
"Chicken soup in every pot and
nickel slots in every garage."

00:01:19.467 --> 00:01:20.601
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.601 --> 00:01:21.934
It was a big announcement.

00:01:21.934 --> 00:01:23.634
When history looks back
at our great achievements

00:01:23.634 --> 00:01:24.901
in healthcare, they'll think,

00:01:24.901 --> 00:01:26.868
Lyndon Johnson's
Medicare and Medicaid,

00:01:26.868 --> 00:01:28.534
Obama's Affordable Care Act,

00:01:28.534 --> 00:01:30.767
and now Trump's plastic coupon.

00:01:30.767 --> 00:01:32.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:34.567
I think Trump might be out of
touch with the average American,

00:01:34.567 --> 00:01:36.400
'cause if there's one thing
people don't need

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:38.601
it's another savings card
on their key chain.

00:01:38.601 --> 00:01:40.400
It's like, "Are you a member?"

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:43.000
"Ah. I'm not."
"You want to be?"

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:45.033
"I-I really don't."

00:01:45.033 --> 00:01:46.834
"It only takes
about 45 minutes."

00:01:46.834 --> 00:01:49.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:49.767 --> 00:01:52.234
Trump's like everyone who waits
too long to order a present

00:01:52.234 --> 00:01:53.934
and then panic-buys a gift card.

00:01:53.934 --> 00:01:58.334
Like, "Oh, gosh.
Do they go to Bass Pro Shops?

00:01:58.334 --> 00:02:00.234
Sure."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.234 --> 00:02:02.367
On top of the discount card,
Trump also signed

00:02:02.367 --> 00:02:04.367
an executive order
to protect people

00:02:04.367 --> 00:02:09.601
with preexisting conditions,
which is already in Obamacare.

00:02:09.601 --> 00:02:11.734
That's like the new C.E.O.
of Olive Garden saying,

00:02:11.734 --> 00:02:13.767
"And I'm happy to introduce
my new idea --

00:02:13.767 --> 00:02:18.133
unlimited breadsticks."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.133 --> 00:02:21.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:21.467 --> 00:02:23.300
Speaking of the President,
this is going viral.

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:26.968
A CNN reporter snapped a photo
of a duplex in Dallas

00:02:26.968 --> 00:02:29.200
where one side is covered
in Biden flags,

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:31.100
the other side
is decked out for Trump.

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:32.534
Take a look at this.
This is real.

00:02:32.534 --> 00:02:33.968
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.968 --> 00:02:35.434
Yeah, even crazier,

00:02:35.434 --> 00:02:37.634
there's an undecided voter
living in the chimney.

00:02:37.634 --> 00:02:39.667
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.667 --> 00:02:40.834
That's pretty over-the-top.

00:02:40.834 --> 00:02:42.968
Even people who bought
the 12-foot skeleton

00:02:42.968 --> 00:02:45.100
from Home Depot were like,
"Y'all need to tone it down."

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:46.567
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.567 --> 00:02:48.100
Listen to this --
an exhibit just opened

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:50.300
at the Richard Nixon
presidential library

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:54.434
that reveals Trump and Nixon
were pen pals in the 1980s.

00:02:54.434 --> 00:02:57.501
Yeah, it's pretty historic.
Here are some of the letters.

00:02:57.501 --> 00:02:58.734
♪♪

00:02:58.734 --> 00:03:01.968
-"Dear Mr. President,
you're one of my idols.

00:03:01.968 --> 00:03:03.634
Next time
you're in New York City,

00:03:03.634 --> 00:03:06.200
I'd be honored
if you stay at Trump Tower.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:08.467
I can get us tickets
to "Starlight Express,"

00:03:08.467 --> 00:03:11.667
a spectacular Broadway show
about singing trains.

00:03:11.667 --> 00:03:13.701
Really thought-provoking stuff.

00:03:13.701 --> 00:03:16.901
Yours, Donald."

00:03:16.901 --> 00:03:20.200
-"Dear Donald, so happy
to receive your letter.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:23.300
You remind me of myself
if I were 30 years younger,

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:26.067
not as bright,
but also not as paranoid,

00:03:26.067 --> 00:03:28.400
and had the exact same ego.

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:30.667
Have you thought of running
for president one day?

00:03:30.667 --> 00:03:33.734
Best regards, Richard.

00:03:33.734 --> 00:03:37.133
-"Dear Richard, I have
considered being president.

00:03:37.133 --> 00:03:40.667
Either that or a game-show host.
Keeping my options open.

00:03:40.667 --> 00:03:43.567
My only fear of being president
would be screwing up

00:03:43.567 --> 00:03:45.667
and leaving the White House
in disgrace.

00:03:45.667 --> 00:03:48.300
Best, Don Don."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:51.767
-Dear Don Don, that's the
mistake I made -- leaving.

00:03:51.767 --> 00:03:53.200
The secret is to stay in office

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:55.334
no matter how many scandals
you have.

00:03:55.334 --> 00:03:58.334
And here's a hot tip -- even if
you're voted out of office,

00:03:58.334 --> 00:04:00.334
you can always refuse to leave.

00:04:00.334 --> 00:04:02.300
With any luck, one day you too

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:04.968
will be lurching through the
White House halls like an ogre,

00:04:04.968 --> 00:04:08.434
despised by America,
continuing the work I started.

00:04:08.434 --> 00:04:10.567
Your friend, Dicky Baby."

00:04:10.567 --> 00:04:13.567
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:13.567 --> 00:04:17.434
-"Dear --
Dear Don Don."

00:04:17.434 --> 00:04:19.100
[ Laughter ]

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:21.467
Oh, I saw, you guys,
that United Airlines is taking

00:04:21.467 --> 00:04:23.767
a big step to try
and get people flying again.

00:04:23.767 --> 00:04:25.200
Check out their plan.

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:27.567
-United is the first
U.S. airline to roll out

00:04:27.567 --> 00:04:29.601
a COVID testing program
for passengers

00:04:29.601 --> 00:04:31.634
starting October 15th.

00:04:31.634 --> 00:04:34.834
Bay Area flyers bound for Hawaii
will be given the option

00:04:34.834 --> 00:04:36.534
to order an at-home testing kit

00:04:36.534 --> 00:04:39.267
or reserve a time for
a rapid test at the airport.

00:04:39.267 --> 00:04:42.400
-It's like United looked
at the TSA line and thought,

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:44.033
"What if we probed even deeper?"

00:04:44.033 --> 00:04:48.133
[ Laughter ]

00:04:48.133 --> 00:04:50.400
Meanwhile, if you test positive,
you can still fly.

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:51.567
They just give you a pillow

00:04:51.567 --> 00:04:53.234
and stuff you
in the overhead compartment.

00:04:53.234 --> 00:04:54.801
[ Laughter ]

00:04:54.801 --> 00:04:57.634
In sports news,
it was a big night for NBC

00:04:57.634 --> 00:05:01.033
'cause tonight was game 4
of the Stanley Cup finals...

00:05:01.033 --> 00:05:02.367
[ cheers and applause ]

00:05:02.367 --> 00:05:06.701
...with Tampa Bay and Dallas
facing off in Edmonton.

00:05:06.701 --> 00:05:10.167
Tampa Bay's enforcers have been
unstoppable this season.

00:05:10.167 --> 00:05:13.234
Hey, you guys know what
an enforcer does, right?

00:05:13.234 --> 00:05:14.901
Just checking.
-[ Whistle blows ]

00:05:14.901 --> 00:05:17.000
[ Groans ]

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:18.934
Sorry there, Jimmy,
I'mma have to send you back

00:05:18.934 --> 00:05:21.334
to the penalty box for that one.

00:05:21.334 --> 00:05:23.334
-Come on!

00:05:23.334 --> 00:05:25.334
[ Laughter ]

00:05:28.367 --> 00:05:31.601
-Ooh, this has got to be
disappointing for Fallon,

00:05:31.601 --> 00:05:34.400
whose monologue was on fire
right up till that last joke.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:36.133
[ Laughter ]
Here's hoping this penalty

00:05:36.133 --> 00:05:39.000
doesn't derail him too badly
for the rest of the show.

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:42.534
Let's see what happens.

00:05:42.534 --> 00:05:44.968
[ Buzzer ]

00:05:44.968 --> 00:05:46.300
-Um...

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:49.501
[ Laughter ]

00:05:52.667 --> 00:05:55.200
-Tonight was game 4
of the Stanley Cup finals.

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:56.667
[ Laughter ]

00:05:56.667 --> 00:05:58.334
Tampa Bay and Dallas facing off.

00:05:58.334 --> 00:05:59.701
It's pretty exciting
'cause the last time

00:05:59.701 --> 00:06:02.968
Texas and Florida got together,
truck nuts were born.

00:06:02.968 --> 00:06:06.234
[ Laughter ]

00:06:06.234 --> 00:06:08.300
Well, this is interesting.
Amazon just unveiled

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:10.133
a new kind
of home-security camera

00:06:10.133 --> 00:06:11.300
that I've never really
seen before.

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:12.501
Watch this.

00:06:12.501 --> 00:06:14.901
-Amazon announcing
a new Ring security camera

00:06:14.901 --> 00:06:17.901
that is fixed on top
of a flying drone.

00:06:17.901 --> 00:06:19.767
It's meant to fly
through your house

00:06:19.767 --> 00:06:21.834
when you're not there
and record footage,

00:06:21.834 --> 00:06:24.534
show you what's going on there.

00:06:24.534 --> 00:06:25.968
-I actually think
this is a great invention.

00:06:25.968 --> 00:06:27.801
It's way better
than what I usually do.

00:06:27.801 --> 00:06:30.067
GoPro tied to a ceiling fan.

00:06:30.067 --> 00:06:33.400
[ Laughter ]

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:35.133
Meanwhile, every nanny saw that
and was like,

00:06:35.133 --> 00:06:36.968
"I get it.
You don't trust me."

00:06:36.968 --> 00:06:38.567
[ Laughter ]

00:06:38.567 --> 00:06:41.133
"Find someone else."

00:06:41.133 --> 00:06:43.601
Here's some good news for
restaurants in New York City.

00:06:43.601 --> 00:06:44.901
Listen to this.

00:06:44.901 --> 00:06:47.334
-Outdoor dining is becoming
permanent year 'round.

00:06:47.334 --> 00:06:49.300
Mayor de Blasio
making that announcement,

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:51.067
but he's also making
the open restaurants

00:06:51.067 --> 00:06:53.100
initiative permanent,
so that means the streets

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:55.901
and sidewalk areas blocked off
for dining right now

00:06:55.901 --> 00:06:59.234
are going to stay that way.
-Yeah, open year 'round.

00:06:59.234 --> 00:07:01.167
Be a little tricky
in the winter.

00:07:01.167 --> 00:07:02.834
The waiter will give you
a basket of warm rolls

00:07:02.834 --> 00:07:05.067
and then turn away while you
stuff them in your pants.

00:07:05.067 --> 00:07:09.467
[ Laughter ]

00:07:09.467 --> 00:07:11.367
On the bright side,
you won't need a steak knife.

00:07:11.367 --> 00:07:12.667
You can just use your nipples.

00:07:12.667 --> 00:07:16.000
[ Laughter ]

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:18.167
Speaking of New York City,
officials just found something

00:07:18.167 --> 00:07:20.167
pretty interesting
in one of the storage rooms

00:07:20.167 --> 00:07:22.567
at Grand Central Station.
Check this out.

00:07:22.567 --> 00:07:24.834
-Three transit employees
are accused of

00:07:24.834 --> 00:07:26.901
turning a storage room
at Grand Central Station

00:07:26.901 --> 00:07:29.467
into their own personal
man-cave.

00:07:29.467 --> 00:07:33.701
Officials say they found
a futon, a large flat-screen TV,

00:07:33.701 --> 00:07:37.801
a fridge, workout equipment,
even an A.C.

00:07:37.801 --> 00:07:40.167
[ Laughter ]
-What?

00:07:40.167 --> 00:07:43.400
-Hey, could we see that couch
in that man-cave again?

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:46.467
[ Laughter ]
Oh, gosh.

00:07:46.467 --> 00:07:47.767
The only thing that belongs
on that couch

00:07:47.767 --> 00:07:49.634
is a giant bedbug
smoking a cigarette.

00:07:49.634 --> 00:07:51.667
[ Inhales ]
"Want a beer?"

00:07:51.667 --> 00:07:53.300
[ Laughter ]

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:56.167
That isn't a futon, it's
actually one giant sleeping rat.

00:07:56.167 --> 00:07:58.033
[ Laughter ]

00:07:58.033 --> 00:08:00.467
Actually, that bed is --
that's where they take you

00:08:00.467 --> 00:08:01.801
if you book
the presidential suite

00:08:01.801 --> 00:08:03.434
at the Times Square
Hampton Inn.

00:08:03.434 --> 00:08:05.334
It's true.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:05.334 --> 00:08:07.701
And, finally, guys, journalists
have a tough job these days,

00:08:07.701 --> 00:08:09.534
and there's been so many great
TV reporters

00:08:09.534 --> 00:08:10.868
working out in the field,

00:08:10.868 --> 00:08:12.567
but because everyone's
wearing face masks,

00:08:12.567 --> 00:08:15.200
we realize it's possible to make
it seem like they're saying,

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:17.367
well, anything.
So with that in mind, it's time

00:08:17.367 --> 00:08:19.868
for another installment
of "Face Mask the Nation."

00:08:19.868 --> 00:08:20.868
Check it out.

00:08:20.868 --> 00:08:25.000
♪ Face mask the nation ♪

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:26.567
-We're gonna talk about
the Arizona Senate race.

00:08:26.567 --> 00:08:27.834
[ Inhales loudly ]

00:08:27.834 --> 00:08:29.667
We discovered every time
I breathe through my mask...

00:08:29.667 --> 00:08:30.701
[ Inhales loudly ]

00:08:30.701 --> 00:08:32.033
...you can see
every breath I take.

00:08:32.033 --> 00:08:33.467
[ Inhales loudly ]

00:08:33.467 --> 00:08:34.801
-You think I got what it takes
for "America's Got Talent"?

00:08:34.801 --> 00:08:35.968
[ Inhales loudly ]

00:08:35.968 --> 00:08:38.267
-So, I show up
to the hospital, and I say,

00:08:38.267 --> 00:08:40.167
"I'd like to volunteer
as a candy striper,"

00:08:40.167 --> 00:08:42.200
and the nurse says,
"It doesn't work that way.

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:45.067
You gotta sign up, and it helps
if you're a high school kid."

00:08:45.067 --> 00:08:48.100
I say, "Look, I got the outfit.
This is my lunch hour.

00:08:48.100 --> 00:08:50.033
Do you want
a candy striper or not?"

00:08:50.033 --> 00:08:52.467
-Am I a "Mortal Kombat"
character? Yes.

00:08:52.467 --> 00:08:55.200
Do I know Scorpion's
finishing move? Of course.

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:57.200
His fatality is a flaming skull.

00:08:57.200 --> 00:08:59.234
Do I know anything
about politics? Yes.

00:08:59.234 --> 00:09:03.234
If by politics you mean arcade
fighting games from the '90s.

00:09:03.234 --> 00:09:05.601
-I tried eating lunch
through my mask the other day,

00:09:05.601 --> 00:09:07.968
and I'll tell you something,
I do not recommend it,

00:09:07.968 --> 00:09:10.467
unless you want a lap
full of soup, Jack!

